# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SANWARNA — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development.
# The app runs with ZERO of these set — the catalog falls back to the
# static data in /data/products.ts, and the admin-only Video Studio is
# simply unreachable (it 500s on missing config rather than opening
# unprotected). Nothing below is required to build, run, or deploy the
# free-tier version of the site.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Site -------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp number for the chat/order buttons (international, no +).
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER="923045519335"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME="SANWARNA"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://sanwarna.vercel.app"

# --- Admin access (Viral Video Studio) ----------------------------------
# The Video Studio (/video-studio) is an internal content-creation tool
# for the brand's team, not a customer-facing feature — it's gated behind
# a simple password-based admin session (see middleware.ts and
# lib/adminAuth.ts). No database or paid auth provider involved: a signed,
# expiring cookie (HMAC-SHA256, Web Crypto API) is issued on successful
# login at /admin/login.
#
# Required to use the Video Studio at all:
ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
# Optional — a separate signing secret for the session cookie. If unset,
# ADMIN_PASSWORD itself is used to sign sessions too (fine for a single
# admin; set this separately if you want to be able to rotate the login
# password without invalidating every other admin's active session).
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=""

# --- Product catalog / database (optional — MotherDuck) -----------------
# By default the catalog lives in /data/products.ts as static TypeScript,
# so the site ships with zero external dependencies and is instant on
# Vercel's edge cache. Set MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN to instead serve the catalog
# from MotherDuck (a managed DuckDB-in-the-cloud service with a free
# tier) — lib/getProducts.ts queries it over MotherDuck's Postgres
# wire-protocol endpoint via the standard `pg` driver, and falls back to
# the static catalog automatically if the query fails or this isn't set.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a free account at https://motherduck.com and a database
#      (default name assumed below is "sanwarna" — create one with that
#      name, or set MOTHERDUCK_DATABASE to match whatever you name it).
#   2. Generate a access token from the MotherDuck UI (Settings -> Tokens)
#      and set it below.
#   3. Run `npm run db:seed` locally (with these vars set) to create the
#      `products` table and load it from /data/products.ts. See
#      sql/schema.sql for the table this creates.
#   4. Set the same variables in your Vercel project's Environment
#      Variables settings so production reads from MotherDuck too.
# (MotherDuck is also available as a one-click Vercel Marketplace
# integration, which sets MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN for you automatically.)
MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN=""
MOTHERDUCK_HOST="pg.us-east-1-aws.motherduck.com"
MOTHERDUCK_DATABASE="sanwarna"

# --- Product photos (Cloudinary, free tier) -----------------------------
# Leave blank to serve photos from /public. Once set, every product photo
# is loaded from Cloudinary instead (see lib/cloudinary.ts).
#   1. Create a free account at https://cloudinary.com
#   2. Copy the cloud name, API key and API secret from the dashboard.
#   3. Run `npm run images:upload` to upload public/images/products.
# Only the cloud name (and folder, if you change it) is needed on Vercel;
# the key and secret are only used by the upload script on your computer.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_FOLDER="sanwarna/products"
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=""
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=""

# --- Payments: JazzCash --------------------------------------------------
# Cash on Delivery needs no setup. JazzCash needs a merchant account
# (https://www.jazzcash.com.pk → Business / Online Payment Gateway). The
# merchant portal gives you these three values. Until they are set, a
# shopper who picks JazzCash is told to use Cash on Delivery instead.
JAZZCASH_MERCHANT_ID=""
JAZZCASH_PASSWORD=""
JAZZCASH_INTEGRITY_SALT=""
# "sandbox" for JazzCash's test system, "live" for real money.
JAZZCASH_ENV="sandbox"
# In the JazzCash portal, set the Return URL to:
#   <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/api/checkout/jazzcash/return

# --- Orders ---------------------------------------------------------------
# With MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN set, every order is saved to the `orders` table in
# MotherDuck and listed at /admin/orders. Optional extra: POST each order
# as JSON to a webhook (Google Sheet script, Slack, Discord, Make, Zapier).
ORDER_WEBHOOK_URL=""

# --- Virtual Try-On -------------------------------------------------------
# The Try-On Studio detects the user's wrist automatically (MediaPipe
# Tasks Vision's HandLandmarker, a free/open-source model that runs
# entirely client-side via WebAssembly — no API key, no server round
# trip, model + WASM fetched from public CDNs on first use) and places
# the cufflink there, with manual drag/scale/rotate controls always
# available as a fallback/override. No configuration is required for
# this — it's on by default. If you later swap in a server-side vision
# API instead, document its key here.
# VISION_API_KEY=""

# --- Viral Video Studio (future upgrade) --------------------------------
# Video generation runs fully in the browser via <canvas> + MediaRecorder
# (WebM, VP9/VP8) — no server render farm, no per-render cost. Optional
# free/open royalty-free audio can be self-hosted in /public/audio. If you
# later add server-side rendering (e.g. for MP4 transcoding via
# ffmpeg.wasm on a background worker, still free/OSS):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VIDEO_RENDER_MODE="client"   # "client" | "server"

# --- Analytics (free tier) ----------------------------------------------
# Vercel Web Analytics / Speed Insights are free on hobby projects.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ANALYTICS="true"
